    <section class="snap-section rd-sec rd-tint rd-faq" id="faq" data-index="4">
      <div class="about-band offers-band"></div>
      <div class="rd-inner">
        <div class="rd-eyebrow">Systemic Therapy &amp; Counseling</div>
        <h2 class="rd-h2">Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <div class="rd-faq-grid">
          <div class="rd-faq-list">
            <div class="rd-faq-item is-active">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="true"><span class="rd-num">01</span><span class="rd-q">How does working together begin?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>It begins with a non-binding, free initial contact by phone or online by video. In about 20 minutes, we get to know each other and clarify the framework.</p><p>This is followed by the in-depth first session. We clarify your concerns and whether it feels right to begin working together. The first session is a regular session and is charged at the usual rates.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">02</span><span class="rd-q">How long does a session last, and how far apart are appointments?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><div class="faq-facts">
                  <div class="faq-fact"><span>Individual</span><strong>from 60 min.</strong></div>
                  <div class="faq-fact"><span>Two or more people</span><strong>from 90 min.</strong></div>
                  <div class="faq-fact"><span>Interval</span><strong>2–4 weeks</strong></div>
                  <div class="faq-fact"><span>Often useful</span><strong>4–12 sessions</strong></div>
                </div>
                <p>I offer individual sessions of 60 minutes or longer. Depending on need, longer appointments can also be agreed, for example 75 or 90 minutes. I offer sessions for two or more people with a minimum duration of 90 minutes. Here, too, longer sessions can be agreed as needed, for example 105 or 120 minutes.</p><p>How many sessions you wish to attend overall depends on your themes and needs. I often work in a brief, solution-oriented way: only as many sessions take place as are meaningful and necessary for your concerns. For deeper processes of change, 4 to 12 sessions are, in my experience, useful.</p><p>We agree on the interval between sessions according to your possibilities; it is usually between 2 and 4 weeks. Some people prefer very different rhythms, and a lot can be arranged. What suits you, we agree at the end of the first session and adjust as needed along the way.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">03</span><span class="rd-q">Do sessions also take place online?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>Sessions take place in Berlin-Moabit (INSA-Berlin · Alt-Moabit 91b) or online by video, in German or English.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">04</span><span class="rd-q">What costs can I expect?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>The hourly rate is 150 euros. You will find all details on session lengths, invoicing and cancellation on the costs page.</p><a class="rd-faq-link" href="{{ '/en/systemische-therapie/kosten/' | url }}">All details on costs, invoicing and cancellation<span class="rd-chev"></span></a></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">05</span><span class="rd-q">Do you offer psychotherapy, and will health insurance reimburse the costs?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>No. My services are expressly not psychotherapy in the clinical sense under the German Psychotherapists Act (Psychotherapeutengesetz) or the Alternative Practitioners Act (Heilpraktikergesetz), but services outside the so-called remit of medical treatment (&ldquo;Heilauftrag&rdquo;). My services are based on my qualifications from recognized further training in Systemic Therapy &amp; Counseling (DGSF), Coaching (DGSv) &amp; Supervision (DGSv/SG). I do not hold a license to practice (Approbation).</p><p>That is why my services are self-pay services, and billing is always directly with you. Statutory and private health insurers do not reimburse them.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item" id="faq-krise">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">06</span><span class="rd-q">Where can I turn in an acute mental health crisis?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>My services do not replace emergency care. If you are in an acute crisis, see yourself or others at risk, or no longer know what to do, please get help immediately:</p>
                <div class="krise-btns">
                  <a class="krise-btn krise-btn-out" href="tel:+49303906310"><strong><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M22 16.92v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.18 2 19.79 19.79 0 0 1-8.63-3.07 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6 19.79 19.79 0 0 1-3.07-8.67A2 2 0 0 1 4.11 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.72c.127.96.361 1.903.7 2.81a2 2 0 0 1-.45 2.11L8.09 9.91a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.27-1.27a2 2 0 0 1 2.11-.45c.907.339 1.85.573 2.81.7A2 2 0 0 1 22 16.92z"/></svg>030 390 63 10</strong><span>Berliner Krisendienst · around the clock</span></a>
                  <a class="krise-btn krise-btn-fill" href="tel:112"><strong><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M22 16.92v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.18 2 19.79 19.79 0 0 1-8.63-3.07 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6 19.79 19.79 0 0 1-3.07-8.67A2 2 0 0 1 4.11 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.72c.127.96.361 1.903.7 2.81a2 2 0 0 1-.45 2.11L8.09 9.91a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.27-1.27a2 2 0 0 1 2.11-.45c.907.339 1.85.573 2.81.7A2 2 0 0 1 22 16.92z"/></svg>112</strong><span>Emergency · in case of acute danger to life</span></a>
                </div>
                <p class="krise-lead">All points of contact at a glance:</p>
                <ul class="rd-faq-ul">
                  <li><strong>Emergency number 112</strong> (rescue service, free of charge): in case of acute danger to life, after a suicide attempt, or in case of acute danger to self or others.</li>
                  <li><strong>Emergency room of the responsible hospital</strong>: In acute mental health crises, you can go directly to the emergency room of a responsible hospital at any time, even without an appointment. You can find an overview of the hospitals obliged to admit patients in Mitte at the <a href="https://www.berlin.de/ba-mitte/politik-und-verwaltung/service-und-organisationseinheiten/qualitaetsentwicklung-planung-und-koordination-des-oeffentlichen-gesundheitsdienstes/psychiatriekoordination/klinische-versorgung-von-psychisch-kranken-erwachsenen-sowie-psychisch-kranken-kindern-und-jugendlichen-in-berlin-mitte-821617.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mitte District Office (Bezirksamt Mitte)</a>.</li>
                  <li><strong>Berliner Krisendienst (Berlin Crisis Service)</strong>: free of charge, anonymous on request, reachable by phone around the clock, and in urgent cases also with a home visit. Phone <a href="tel:+49303906310">030 390 63 10</a> (Mitte and Friedrichshain-Kreuzberg; at night, on weekends and on public holidays, this number connects you to the Berlin emergency service). You can find the numbers for the other districts at <a href="https://www.berliner-krisendienst.de/ich-brauche-hilfe/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">berliner-krisendienst.de</a>.</li>
                  <li><strong>Medical on-call service 116 117</strong>: outside practice opening hours, when symptoms cannot wait until the next day but there is no acute danger to life.</li>
                  <li><strong>TelefonSeelsorge</strong> (telephone counseling): free of charge, anonymous and around the clock at <a href="tel:08001110111">0800 111 0 111</a>, <a href="tel:08001110222">0800 111 0 222</a> or <a href="tel:116123">116 123</a>. Also by chat or email via <a href="https://www.telefonseelsorge.de/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">telefonseelsorge.de</a>.</li>
                  <li><strong>krisenchat</strong> (for people under 25): free of charge and around the clock by chat via WhatsApp or SMS, when writing is easier than speaking. More information at <a href="https://www.krisenchat.de/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">krisenchat.de</a>.</li>
                  <li><strong>General practitioner's office, psychiatric or psychotherapeutic practice, and the Social Psychiatric Service (Sozialpsychiatrischer Dienst) of your district</strong>: during the day, when the situation is not acutely life-threatening. You can find the contact for the Social Psychiatric Service on your district office's website.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>Further information is provided by the <a href="https://gesund.bund.de/wege-im-gesundheitswesen/erwachsenenleben/psychische-gesundheit/anlaufstellen-bei-psychischen-krisen" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Federal Health Portal (Gesundheitsportal des Bundes)</a>.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">07</span><span class="rd-q">Is the content treated confidentially, and what does the duty of confidentiality mean?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>Your personal data and everything discussed in counseling or therapy are subject to the legal duty of confidentiality. Without your express written consent, I do not pass on any information to third parties. The duty of confidentiality can be lifted only in a few legally defined situations, namely when there is an acute danger to life or limb to yourself or others.</p><p>For quality assurance, I take part in supervision of my own work or teaching supervision in further-training contexts. There I always bring in content anonymized, i.e. no personal data is passed on.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">08</span><span class="rd-q">Am I welcome with you, regardless of relationship form, gender identity and sexual orientation?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>Yes. Everyone is welcome to work with me. Gender identity and sexual orientation are marked by diversity, and relationships and families can take different forms: as a couple, as a multi-person constellation or as a family.</p><p>In my work, what matters most is how the people involved can shape contact, understanding and connection with one another.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">09</span><span class="rd-q">What does &ldquo;systemic&rdquo; mean in therapy and counseling?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>Systemic work looks at people in their relationships and contexts and focuses on strengths and solutions. You can read more about this above in the section <a href="#arbeitsverstaendnis">&ldquo;My professional understanding&rdquo;</a>.</p></div></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rd-faq-detail" aria-live="polite"><div class="rd-faq-detail-bar"></div><div class="rd-faq-detail-body"></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

